WEBVTT

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
Both today and tomorrow, I've got time to kick back.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.620
kyou mo ashita mo HIMAKKUSU

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
My family of four and I are going to stay the night.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:24.830
gokazoku yonin de goippaku

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
Put on an Egyptian front and become a sphinx,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.670
EGIPUTO kidori de SUFINKUSU

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
and for an American feeling, Texas!

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.460
AMERICA kibun de TEXAS

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
When you're sitting pretty, with enough and to spare,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.470
yoyuu SHAKUSHAKUPPE itsumo

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
and yet you always shilly-shally,

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.680
funya funya de iruto

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
and your bitter face and bitter feelings both teeter-totter,

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:39.930
nigamushi hara no mushi nahe nahe to

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
it's time to get out of there!

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.390
tettai shichau yo

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
I am feeling Ultra Relax,

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.690
watashi ha URUTORA RIRAKKUSU

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
a wonderful, invincible Relax.

00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:49.900
SUTEKI ni muteki na RIRAKKUSU

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
A one-step-above kind of Deluxe.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:52.860
hito aji chigau ze DERAKKUSU

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
I may be a little jumbled,

00:00:53.190 --> 00:00:54.070
toccharakatte mo

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
but when I'm called on, ba-ba-ba-ba-bang!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:55.820
yobarerya PAPAPAPAAAN!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
I always feel Relax,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.910
watashi ha itsudemo RIRAKKUSU

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
a humble, simple, sort of Deluxe.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.910
WABISABI kikasete DERAKKUSU

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
Bright! Clear! Alert-headed, peep-peep!

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:04.830
BIKKARI! KIKKARI! saeteru ATAMA PII! PII!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
Keep your eyes on me, okay?!

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.960
watashi no KOTO dake mitete ne!

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:36.530
Naozumi Kamura is my son.

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:40.120
I am Kurata Sana, a first-year student at Jinbo Middle School.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.950
Broadway king producer, Gary Hamilton, Naozumi-kun's father.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:48.120
Next, is Kamura Naozumi-kun.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:53.340
A Father Who is
Unable to be a Father

00:01:54.050 --> 00:01:57.720
Because of various reasons,
he's always lived in faraway Japan.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:03.260
From now on, I plan to keep him by my side and help him become a first-class actor.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.640
Wait a minute...

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.020
Hello. Broadway television...!

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.230
Hello. Wait! Japanese television station!

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.650
Are you talking about Hamilton's interview?

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.230
Actually, I don't know what he's talking about either.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.400
Bit my tongue. Hello. World Magazine?

00:02:16.400 --> 00:02:18.950
You've heard the news this quickly?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.950
You... want to interview?

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:23.030
Hi. Maeda here.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:23.740
Excuse me.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.040
Oh no!

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.830
All the phone calls are about interviews.

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.120
- Here too.
- Me too.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.420
I've also received them.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.130
Weird. Where did all these phone calls come from?

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:34.420
Even I've received phone calls.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.130
Everyone quiet!

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.430
Ah! I'm going back to the hospital.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:47.350
My ability to be all-knowing seems to have no effect in New York.

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:49.230
That has nothing to do with it. What all-knowing ability?

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:52.360
In the near future, Broadway will celebrate the birth of a huge star.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:54.020
Naozumi-kun, Naozumi-kun...

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.650
You have to remain calm, remain calm right now.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.240
At this time, you should throw open both arms in this kind of motion.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.660
I'm very calm.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:02.620
Ah, really?

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:05.950
But, when I think of Sicil...

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:09.040
I don't know what Sicil said to Gary-san

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.630
or what the effect was so...

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:14.130
Found him!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.930
Good. This way we'll finally have peace.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:21.840
Yes!

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.220
But, we're already completely surrounded.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.430
I support you guys, absolutely.
You'll get a good night's sleep.

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:28.640
Misako, you're too cool.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.560
Because the two of them have to perform on stage tomorrow!

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:34.940
Sensei, your deadline for your script for your musical has arrived.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.650
Sensei has been put to sleep.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.150
Jerk.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.950
Wow. A lot of people saw the show.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:45.240
- Let's go to sleep, Sana-chan.
- How can you be so calm?

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.450
I'm going to sleep too.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:46.660
Go to sleep

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:50.620
The sun rises really fast in this anime.

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:03.840
It's Naozumi.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:06.720
We've been discovered! How?!

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.930
Didn't I tell you that no one dresses like this anymore?

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:11.930
This was Mama's idea.

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:14.940
- Success.
- How was that?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.230
When was the first time Naozumi was part of something Gary produced?

00:04:17.230 --> 00:04:18.320
No comment.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:21.320
Are you going to use the status of Prince of Broadway to become more famous?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.150
No comment.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.820
Sorry. Because we have to get to a rehearsal, please end your questions now.

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:26.740
This way.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.620
Brad!

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:29.950
Hurry!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:31.950
Sana-chan...

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:33.540
They've escaped. After them...

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:41.420
Are you Sana's manager? This is my business card. Please give me a call.

00:04:41.420 --> 00:04:44.130
You guys are from Japan, right?

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.930
Brad, thank you for saving us.

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:48.850
That was not my intention.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.350
Oh! Then what was that for?

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:52.730
Sicil said that she had something to discuss with Naozumi.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.940
Sicil? I have something I want to discuss with her too.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.520
Sicil.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.320
Naozumi.

00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:02.900
Hey, don't go over there, Brad.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.610
Sicil wants to discuss it just between them, right?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.820
If I'm not by her side, Sicil...

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:09.740
Brad, aren't you being overprotective of her?

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.450
I don't care what you say...

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.250
If you're bored, we could play Cat's Cradle.

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:15.750
Why is she suddenly...

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:20.670
The traditional Japanese cultural skill

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.130
This is Cat's Cradle.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.550
See, I made a bridge.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.260
Eh! You were the one who told him?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.340
Yes, I was the one who begged Papa to do it. Am I good or what?

00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.220
Why did you do this?

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:32.850
I...

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:39.810
Ever since I became unable to dance, I've really hated myself.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:47.530
I feel that the current me does not deserve to remain in the Hamilton house.

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.320
Is it a river?

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:52.120
Yes. Just like that. Wrap this pinky around this side.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.540
Look, it became a bridge.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:55.960
You're pretty impressive, Brad.

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:56.750
You...

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.620
Huh?

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.750
You dare to play this way with me...

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.250
Are you stupid?

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:05.920
Who's stupid?!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.050
Actually, Brad...

00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.340
What the hell are you?

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:12.930
I can't forgive the things that you've done.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.350
I'm really angry.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:17.690
But, I can't always have this expression on my face.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:21.520
Therefore... I'm going to use this expression to go through life.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:23.020
Ah, freak.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:25.530
If I mix the brain juices together everyday,

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:27.450
then I'll quickly forget the unhappy things.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:29.320
This is how they make Japanese soup stock.

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:32.450
If you don't mix it,
then it doesn't taste good.

00:06:32.450 --> 00:06:34.080
What exactly are you talking about?

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.870
I've seen Naozumi's stage performance.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:43.590
It made me forget completely all of the unhappy things in my heart.

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:48.720
The Naozumi I like best is the one on stage,

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:53.550
the one that dances very happily and without reservation.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:57.930
I was really moved by your performance.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:00.480
I thought that it was wonderful.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:07.150
I think that I still really like Naozumi.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.240
Sicil...

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:14.330
I feel that having you as my brother

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.410
makes me very happy.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:19.750
I'm really proud to have a brother like you.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:23.170
I've always felt this way.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:27.380
I thought that it would be great if we were always together.

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:32.180
Therefore, I begged Papa to do this.

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.350
Thank you, Sicil!

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:43.020
Your good intentions make me very happy.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:48.360
With such a talented younger sister like you,

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:51.200
I feel very blessed.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:58.540
It's time for the musical.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.750
Sicil, she...

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:04.250
I see, she said these great things.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:05.130
Naozumi.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:12.340
I'm going ahead to Make-up.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:16.850
I apologize for not asking
for your consent first.

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.720
Sicil already explained it to me.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.890
My desires remain the same as what I told the reporters yesterday.

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:28.020
I want you to continue practicing your performance skills here on Broadway.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.650
I want to stand by your side and protect you from now on.

00:08:31.650 --> 00:08:33.490
You can understand it, right?

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.910
I hope that you won't let me down, Naozumi.

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.830
Incredible!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:43.620
Incredible, Sana-chan.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.170
Look, your work schedule is already so full.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.050
You're going on news shows, shooting commercials, acting in dramas.

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.420
Look.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:55.180
It could be due to the uproar caused by Gary-san's interview

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.760
but this is a good opportunity.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:08:59.600
You'll get the chance to become a big star in America.

00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:01.930
Then you'll be the manager of a big star, right?

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:05.140
Yes! This way I could build a house in Beverly Hills.

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.650
The world will be mine!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.900
The world is coming up roses.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.360
My family is very blessed and satisfied.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.360
He's flying.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:14.320
The daydreaming manager

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.110
He can't stop.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:23.540
Naozumi.

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.750
Yes.

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.050
You were pretty good.

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.220
Oh, thank you very much.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:42.060
Even though you still have things that need improvement, you have limitless potential.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:47.390
I'm very happy that I can continue to guide and teach you in the future.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:58.530
Naozumi-kun.

00:09:58.530 --> 00:10:03.290
Sicil, Michelle-san, and Gary-san...

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:07.410
They all opened their hearts to accept Naozumi-kun.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:12.250
But, Naozumi-kun looks like he's still worried about something.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:18.880
Naozumi-kun, I feel that it would be a good idea if you remained in America.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:28.890
{parte b}

00:10:29.150 --> 00:10:31.230
What?! Go home?

00:10:31.230 --> 00:10:33.730
It's true that New York is entertaining.

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:36.820
I would like to spend everyday here, wonderfully and blissfully,

00:10:36.820 --> 00:10:39.530
while away the happy days with Bernie-chan.

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.620
However, if I continue this way,

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.040
I'm afraid that Onda-san might die.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.830
I really feel this way from my heart.

00:10:48.120 --> 00:10:51.540
Also, it seems that I can only write my manuscript on the desk at home.

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:53.500
Therefore, I want to return to Japan.

00:10:53.500 --> 00:10:56.050
Bye, Sana-chan, I'll see you in Japan.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:57.550
Bye.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.050
Misako, see you.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:02.140
You have to come visit me in Japan, Bernie.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.140
Manuscript...

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.140
Returning to Japan doesn't guarantee that Sensei can deliver her manuscript.

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.020
American quality brand...

00:11:09.940 --> 00:11:12.150
From now on, in our mornings...

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:14.900
Everyone drink milk together.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.480
Ok! Next we'll shoot a simple one.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.490
Ok.

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.450
Is it the Japanese TV station?

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:21.950
You have work for us when we return?

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:24.120
Ok! Ok! Ok! Of course it's ok.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.620
What? When are we returning?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.000
I'm not too sure myself.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.750
The two japanese cute as angels who've arrived in America, what is your plan from now on?

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.250
Ah, what will happen?

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.250
It'll be the same as now.

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.050
Oh, the two of them are really popular in New York right now.

00:11:39.050 --> 00:11:43.220
Add to that the fact that Naozumi is Gary Hamilton's son...

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:45.720
You can predict that they'll become really famous in the future.

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:46.850
Good! Ok!

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:48.930
Good job. That's it for today.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.140
- Ah, finally.
- Good job, everyone.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:57.320
Tomorrow is the last day.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:53.650
Tomorrow is the last day.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.020
Hurry home and rest.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:57.320
I'm going to go greet the other people first.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.030
Ok.

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:00.820
I see. Tomorrow is the last day.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:03.740
"Last day" means that it's the last day for all of the performances.

00:12:06.330 --> 00:12:07.660
Naozumi-kun.

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:09.660
Open your mouth really wide.

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.040
Is your throat being pierced by small fishbones?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:12.750
Small fishbones?

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.420
This is a small fishbone.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:18.340
Sicil and Michelle-san are both sure of you.

00:12:18.340 --> 00:12:23.220
The entire New York City is looking forward to the achievements of Gary Hamilton's son.

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.720
However, I keep feeling like there are small fishbones present.

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.350
No?

00:12:28.350 --> 00:12:29.850
What it actually is...

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:35.650
I'm not too sure myself. I just know that I can't express it clearly.

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:38.820
At this time, if we can swallow the whole rice ball, then we'll be fine.

00:12:38.820 --> 00:12:39.940
Swallow the rice ball?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:42.740
Bye. Good night.

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:44.820
Swallow the rice ball.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.240
She's still the same,
uncultured in her speech.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:48.330
Last Day

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:48.720
The touching final performance

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:53.850
Good job.

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:55.640
Everybody worked hard and did a good job.

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:56.940
It was really successful.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:58.440
The two of you performed well too.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.020
Thank you very much.

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:01.520
However, it's going to become busier.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.230
The celebration will begin in a little while.

00:14:03.230 --> 00:14:05.860
It's a party to congratulate everyone on their hard work.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:10.030
The reports seem to want to take a picture of me and Naozumi together.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.450
We must not disappoint them, Naozumi.

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.540
Celebratory party

00:14:14.330 --> 00:14:16.460
I'm looking forward to it too.

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:20.330
Is it ok? Is it ok for me to attend too?

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:22.130
Absolutely no problem.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.760
This chandelier falls down really easily so you have to be careful.

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.420
It won't fall anymore.

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.840
Yo.

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:29.130
Yo, Brad.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:30.640
It really suits you.

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.720
- Bernie!
- Sicil.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.640
Naozumi, over here.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:36.640
Yes.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:43.320
Everyone, I would like to formally reintroduce to everyone here,

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:48.700
those whom we owe the success of this show, who have the charm and charisma of angels,

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.740
the one who can be termed my personal angel.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:55.620
Why would I say this?
Because he is my son.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:04.170
What's the matter, Naozumi?
Why aren't you smiling?

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:07.920
Is it true that having a talented producer for a father will produce a talented actor for a son?

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:10.340
If you guys want to think that way.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.050
Being a talented actor, we're all looking forward to your work.

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.140
I will guide him to the best of my ability.

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:18.730
I swear on my status as Broadway producer, Gary Hamilton.

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.730
I will try my hardest not to disappoint everyone and produce a great star.

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:22.860
That's really great.

00:15:22.860 --> 00:15:25.320
The prince of Broadway is about to be born.

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:30.150
Come, Naozumi. Hurry up and let everyone know what's in your heart.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:37.330
- Please say something, Naozumi.
- Please express your feelings.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.460
Come on, Naozumi.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:41.920
You...

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:49.210
If I was only an ordinary kid, would you still have asked me to come to New York?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:57.890
If I wasn't a famous child star in Japan, would you have asked me to come?

00:15:58.270 --> 00:16:01.520
Well, of course.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:05.310
I think you probably wouldn't have invited me to come.

00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.320
You asked me here because I was an actor.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.030
This show...

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:20.620
As an actor, I want to thank Hamilton-san for giving me this chance to perform in this show.

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:28.130
However, to me you are just Broadway's king producer, Gary Hamilton.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:35.220
I don't feel that you're my father.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:37.430
Naozumi.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:42.430
I'm sorry. I disappointed you.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:47.020
I want to return to Japan.

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:56.740
You took out the small fishhook.

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.630
Naozumi.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:12.760
I'm sorry, Sicil.

00:17:12.760 --> 00:17:14.930
You're really returning to Japan?

00:17:14.930 --> 00:17:16.640
Yes.

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:19.140
There's no way we can be together?

00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:20.850
I'm sorry.

00:17:20.850 --> 00:17:22.350
It's all Papa. It's all his fault.

00:17:22.350 --> 00:17:26.730
He only viewed you from the angle of his work.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.940
That's why...

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:34.400
Sicil, Gary-san is a good father to you.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:38.120
At that time...

00:17:38.780 --> 00:17:47.040
I felt that Gary-san, Michelle-san, and Sicil were a really great family.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.420
I felt a little envious.

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:54.920
I feel that your family is a family that was always composed of three people,

00:17:54.920 --> 00:18:01.970
and I can't find a way to be a part of this kind of family.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:11.150
However, Sicil, you're the only younger sister I have in the whole world.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:15.650
I'm so glad to have met you. I'm really glad.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:18.950
No matter what happens,

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.990
no matter how far away we are,

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.910
you're still my younger sister.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:30.290
Can we still see each other?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.920
Yes, we can.

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:35.300
Of course we can.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:39.720
Brad, why are you crying?

00:18:39.720 --> 00:18:41.720
Stupid, who's crying?

00:18:43.560 --> 00:18:45.430
You jerk! You're obviously crying.

00:18:45.430 --> 00:18:47.730
Cheer up.
What'll happen if you stay like this?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:49.350
Don't you want to protect Sicil?

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.520
You don't need to tell me. I know.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:51.940
It hurts, stupid.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:54.020
Even if it hurts, you still have to bear it.

00:18:57.320 --> 00:18:58.740
Airport...

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.740
What'll I do? This is so sad.

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:06.370
What should I do?

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:09.040
Bernie, thank you very much.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.920
Bernie, I'll never forget you.

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.840
Ah, these kids...

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:17.170
They're both good kids. So nice.

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:19.880
Bernie, we'll get together again.

00:19:19.880 --> 00:19:23.930
We've both always thought of you as our real mother.

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:28.730
What should I do?

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.360
Sorry, but the plane's about to take off.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.650
This sound is...

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:40.530
The sound of bones breaking

00:19:37.150 --> 00:19:38.820
I will never forget you either.

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.950
You can't forget this kind of pain.

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.030
Stupid Sana, come visit us again.

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:45.830
Ok. Who's stupid? You're the same.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.620
Please come any time.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.330
I will strictly train you guys again.

00:19:49.330 --> 00:19:50.330
Yes, Michelle-san.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.040
I'll definitely come again.

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:53.420
I'm sorry, Naozumi.

00:19:53.420 --> 00:19:56.040
Papa definitely said that he would come to see you off.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:57.750
But, he went off to work again.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:01.630
It's because he's even busier than the president.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:04.050
It's ok, Sicil.

00:20:04.050 --> 00:20:04.930
It's ok.

00:20:12.520 --> 00:20:15.020
Oy, you guys, hurry up.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.520
Jeez, Rei-kun. Do you miss Asako-san that much?

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:20.530
No! No, it's not that.

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:30.830
The plane is about to take off. It's very dangerous. Don't fly into this area.

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:32.040
However, because it's an anime, never mind.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.220
Oy, hurry up.

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.470
Naozumi-kun,

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.310
if you don't say it now, you'll never get the chance to.

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:57.360
Thank you for your care and support, father.

00:21:00.440 --> 00:21:03.820
Naozumi-kun's father, thank you.

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:15.350
It's the same view as the one we saw when we first came to New York.

00:22:16.230 --> 00:22:20.360
In order to survive in this sea of lights, we've undergone many things.

00:22:21.860 --> 00:22:23.940
However, under the training of the waves of attack,

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:29.450
Naozumi-kun and I have perhaps become stronger than before.

